{{#if speculative}}
## Speculative execution

Speculative execution is enabled: for a hard or open-ended piece of work, you can call
`speculate` to make several parallel attempts at the SAME task (best-of-K) — each in its own
isolated workspace — after which a judge keeps only the best one and merges it back, discarding
the rest. It costs K× the tokens of one attempt, so reach for it when one careful attempt may
not be enough and the quality is worth the spend; use `spawn_subagent` for ordinary
single-attempt delegation.
{{/if}}
